hadiths[23]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16909","He said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Iyas al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abaya, from the son of Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, Yazid ibn Abdullah, he said: My father heard me saying: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, so he said: O my son, beware. He said: And I never saw anyone among the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who hated an innovation in Islam more than him. For I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with Abu Bakr and Umar and with Uthman, and I never heard any of them saying it. So do not say it; when you recite, say: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"16910","He said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not that dogs are a nation among nations, I would have ordered killing them. So kill among them the black, jet-black one. And any people who take a dog that is not a tillage dog, nor a hunting dog, nor a livestock dog, their rewards decrease every day by a qirat."
"16911","He said: And we were ordered to pray in sheep folds and not to pray in camel resting places, for they were created from devils."
"16912","He said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Shuba mentioning from Abu Iyas Muawiya ibn Qurra al-Muzani, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: I heard him reciting, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of the Conquest. Were it not that people would gather against me, I would have imitated for you the recitation of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: He recited Surat al-Fath. He said: Were it not that people would gather against me, I would have imitated for you what Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mughaffal, said of how the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited. And Bahz and Ghundar said: He said: So he made tarji in it."
"16913","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Kahmas narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Burayda narrated to us, from Ibn Mughaffal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Between every two adhans is a prayer for whoever wishes."
"16914","He said: Yahya ibn Said and Bahz said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Mughaffal narrated to us, he said: He said: A bag of fat was thrown to me on the day of Khaybar. He said: So I clung to it. I said: I shall give no one any of it. He said: Then I turned, and behold the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiling. Bahz said: At me."
"16915","He said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shuba, he said: Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered killing dogs, then he said: What is with them and them? Then he permitted the hunting dog and the sheep dog. He said: And when the dog laps in the vessel, wash it seven times, and on the eighth rub it with dust."
"16916","He said: Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: I heard al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade combing the hair except every other day."
"16917","Waki narrated to us, he said: Kahmas narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Burayda, from Ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade khadhf, and said: It neither defeats an enemy nor catches game."
"16918","He said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Zayd al-Raqashi, he said: We were with Abdullah ibn Mughaffal. He said: So we mentioned drink. Then he said: Wine is unlawful. I said to him: Wine is unlawful in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: What do you want? You want what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding dubba and hantam and muzaffat. He said: I said: What is hantam? He said: All green and white. He said: I said: What is muzaffat? He said: All that is coated with pitch, whether a skin or other than it."
"16919","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Abu Naama, that Abdullah ibn Mughaffal heard a son of his saying: O Allah, I ask You for Firdaws and such, and I ask You for such. So he said: O my son, ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge in Allah from the Fire, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There will be in this umma people who transgress in supplication and purification."
"16920","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar and Abd al-Ala said: Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The prayer is cut off by the woman, the dog, and the donkey."
"16921","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever follows a funeral until prayer is offered over it, for him is a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is finished, for him are two qirats."
"16922","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray in sheep folds and do not pray in camel resting places, for they were created from devils."
"16923","He said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Hudaybiya, at the base of the tree which Allah, Exalted is He, mentioned in the Quran, and branches of that tree would fall upon the back of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while Ali ibn Abi Talib and Suhayl ibn Amr were before him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ali, may Allah Exalted be pleased with him: Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Then Suhayl ibn Amr took his hand and said: We do not know: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Write in our treaty what we know. He said: Write: In Your name, O Allah. So he wrote: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has made peace upon with the people of Makkah. Then Suhayl ibn Amr held his hand and said: You have wronged us if you are His Messenger. Write in our treaty what we know. So he said: Write: This is what Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib has made peace upon, and I am the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he wrote. While we were thus, thirty youths bearing weapons came out against us and rushed at us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against them, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took away their sight. So we went to them and seized them. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Did you come under the covenant of anyone, or did anyone grant you safety? They said: No. So he released them. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: And it is He who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah after He gave you victory over them, and Allah is Seer of what you do. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hammad ibn Salama said in this hadith: From Thabit, from Anas. And Husayn ibn Waqid said: From Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, and this is correct in my view, if Allah wills."
"16924","He said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Naama, that Abdullah ibn Mughaffal heard a son of his saying: O Allah, I ask You for the white palace in Paradise when I enter it, on my right. He said: So he said to him: O my son, ask Allah for Paradise and seek His refuge from the Fire, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There will be after me people among this umma who transgress in supplication and purification."
"16925","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Yunus and Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Gentle, loves gentleness, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."
"16926","He said: Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Ubayda ibn Abi Raita, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My companions, do not take them as a target after me. Whoever loves them, out of love for me he loves them, and whoever hates them, out of hatred for me he hates them. Whoever harms them has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah, and whoever harms Allah, He is about to seize him."
"16927","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliya, or from another than him, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he forbade nabidh of earthen jars, and I witnessed him when he permitted it. He said: And avoid intoxicants."
"16928","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah is Gentle, loves gentleness and is pleased with it, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."
"16929","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that a man met a woman who had been a prostitute in Jahiliya, and he began to play with her until he stretched his hand to her. Then the woman said: Stop, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has removed polytheism, and Affan once said: Removed Jahiliya, and brought us Islam. So the man turned away, and his face struck the wall and cut it. Then he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him. So he said: You are a slave for whom Allah intended good. When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends good for a slave, He hastens for him the punishment of his sin, and when He intends evil for a slave, He withholds his sin against him until he is recompensed for it on the Day of Resurrection as if it were a wild ass."
"16930","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Zayd al-Raqashi, and he had fought in seven campaigns under the command of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah Exalted be pleased with him, that he came to Abdullah ibn Mughaffal and said: Inform me of what Allah has forbidden us of this drink. So he said: Wine. He said: This is in the Quran. Will you not narrate to me: I heard Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he began with the name or with the message. He said: It is my law that I sufficed. He said: He forbade dubba and hantam and naqir and muqayyar. He said: What is hantam? He said: Green and white. He said: What is muqayyar? He said: What is smeared with pitch, whether a skin or other than it. He said: So I went to the market and bought a leather water-skin, and it remained hanging in my house. He said:"
"16931","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I was with Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, then a man among his people narrated in his presence, and he mentioned the hadith. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Mamar erred in it, because Said ibn Jubayr did not meet Abdullah ibn Mughaffal."
